{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <cmath>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef unsigned long long ull;\ntypedef pair<int, int> pii;\ntypedef pair<ll, ll> pll;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint n, S, cnt[250], id[250];\nint f[10][250];\nvector<int> vec[10];\nmap<pll, int> dpMemo;\n\nint modExp(int base, int exp) {\n    int res = 1;\n    base %= MOD;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = (1LL * res * base) % MOD;\n        base = (1LL * base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint compute(int pos, ll state) {\n    if (state == 0) return 0;\n    if (pos == n) return 1;\n    \n    pll key = make_pair(pos, state);\n    if (dpMemo.find(key) != dpMemo.end()) return dpMemo[key];\n    \n    S++;\n    int total = 0;\n    \n    for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {\n        ll nextSt = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < vec[pos].size(); i++) {\n            if (!(state & (1LL << i))) continue;\n            int prev = vec[pos][i];\n            for (int b = 0; b < n; b++) {\n                if ((mask & (1 << b)) && !(prev & (1 << b))) {\n                    nextSt |= 1LL << id[prev | (1 << b)];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        total = (total + 1LL * f[pos][mask] * compute(pos + 1, nextSt)) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    return dpMemo[key] = total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    int inv100 = modExp(100, MOD - 2);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        f[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            int P;\n            cin >> P;\n            int p1 = (1LL * P * inv100) % MOD;\n            int p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); k++) {\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p1) % MOD;\n                f[i][k] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p0) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); i++) {\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i >> 1] + (i & 1);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); i++) {\n        vec[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    \n    cout << compute(0, 1) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mod_exp(base, exp):\n    res = 1\n    base %= MOD\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            res = (res * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    inv100 = mod_exp(100, MOD - 2)\n    \n    f = [[0] * (1 << n) for _ in range(n)]\n    idx = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        f[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(n):\n            P = int(data[idx])\n            idx += 1\n            p1 = (P * inv100) % MOD\n            p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD\n            for k in range(1 << j):\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (f[i][k] * p1) % MOD\n                f[i][k] = (f[i][k] * p0) % MOD\n    \n    cnt = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        cnt[i] = cnt[i >> 1] + (i & 1)\n    \n    vec = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    id_map = [0] * (1 << n)\n    \n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        vec[cnt[i]].append(i)\n        id_map[i] = len(vec[cnt[i]]) - 1\n    \n    dp_memo = {}\n    \n    def compute(pos, state):\n        if state == 0:\n            return 0\n        if pos == n:\n            return 1\n        \n        key = (pos, state)\n        if key in dp_memo:\n            return dp_memo[key]\n        \n        total = 0\n        for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n            next_st = 0\n            for i in range(len(vec[pos])):\n                if not (state & (1 << i)):\n                    continue\n                prev = vec[pos][i]\n                for b in range(n):\n                    if (mask & (1 << b)) and not (prev & (1 << b)):\n                        next_st |= 1 << id_map[prev | (1 << b)]\n            \n            total = (total + f[pos][mask] * compute(pos + 1, next_st)) % MOD\n        \n        dp_memo[key] = total\n        return total\n    \n    print(compute(0, 1))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00015817821258679032, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.002203062642365694, -0.0001984637783607468, -0.00033778208307921886, -0.08014507591724396, -0.2881097197532654, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.622600959512056e-06, -0.006076314952224493, -0.478767454624176, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.00023112009512260556, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.529942543740617e-06, -2.062299427052494e-05, -0.0025158440694212914, -0.00020013237372040749, -0.14290472865104675, -3.814689989667386e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3